    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="1266" n="1244" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg1244"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of State Atomic Energy Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Truman
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-06">May 6, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You will recall that the Secretary spoke with you about a meeting of the Combined
                    Policy Committee at which there was discussion regarding the meaning of the
                    memorandum of November 16 initialed by you and the Prime Ministers of the United
                    Kingdom and Canada. This involves interpretation of the phrase “full and
                    effective cooperation in the field of atomic energy”. The attached letter from
                    Mr. Stone, Counselor of the Canadian Embassy, is directed to that point. Mr.
                    Stone and the Canadian Ambassador have told me that Mr. Attlee communicated with
                    Mr. Mackenzie King urging him to take a strong position on the interpretation of
                    this document. Mr. King declined to do so and this letter is, I believe, a
                    method of escaping from the predicament of undertaking any interpretation at
                    all.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dean Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d625-a1.xml" xpointer="d625-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
